<node id="hierba:trachyspermum-ammi-ajowan"><data key="n_label">Ajowan, Bishop’S Weed</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_description">Sinónimos: Ammi copticum L., Carum ajowan ined., Carum copticum (L.) C. B. Clarke, Sison ammi L., T. copticum (L.) Link</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">AJOWAN, BISHOP’S WEED</data><data key="n_page">6</data><data key="n_scientific">Trachyspermum ammi (L.) Sprague ex Turrill.</data><data key="n_safety">+++</data><data key="n_safety_raw">+++</data><data key="n_dosages">3–6 g powdered seed; 125 mg extract (KAP).</data><data key="n_extracts">EO fungitoxic at 500 ppm (FFJ4(1) 1:1), also spasmogenic (MPI). Rich in thymol, which could impart many of its biological activities.</data></node>
