<node id="hierba:mentha-canadensis-l-american-corn-mint"><data key="n_label">American Corn Mint, Canadian Mint, Japanese Mint</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_description">Sinónimos: M. arvensis var. glabrata Fernald, M. arvensis var. piperascens Malinv. ex L. H. Bailey</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">AMERICAN CORN MINT, CANADIAN MINT, JAPANESE MINT</data><data key="n_page">21</data><data key="n_scientific">Mentha canadensis L.</data><data key="n_safety">++</data><data key="n_safety_raw">++</data><data key="n_downsides">Commission E reports contraindications for EO: biliary obstruction, gallbladder inflammation, severe liver damage; adverse effects: gastric complaints. Not to be inhaled by small children (AEH).</data></node>
