<node id="hierba:panax-quinquefolius-l-american-ginseng"><data key="n_label">American Ginseng, Ginseng</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">AMERICAN GINSENG, GINSENG</data><data key="n_page">22</data><data key="n_scientific">Panax quinquefolius L.</data><data key="n_safety">+++</data><data key="n_safety_raw">+++</data><data key="n_downsides">Class 1 (AHP). Not covered exactly in PH2 where, unfortunately, they list American (P. quinquefolius) and Siberian Ginseng (Eleutherococcus senticosus) among the trade names for oriental ginseng (Panax ginseng), rendering the entire PH2 entry suspect.</data></node>
