<node id="hierba:veratrum-viride-aiton-american-hellebore"><data key="n_label">American Hellebore</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_description">Sinónimos: V. eschscholtzii A. Gray, V. lobelianum var. eschscholtzianum Schult. &amp; Schult. f.</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">AMERICAN HELLEBORE</data><data key="n_page">23</data><data key="n_scientific">Veratrum viride Aiton</data><data key="n_safety">X</data><data key="n_safety_raw">X</data><data key="n_dosages">0.3–2 ml tincture (1:10)/day (HHB; PHR); 60–240 mg fl extract; 120–600 mg tincture (MAD). Old daily dose 100 mg (PH2).</data><data key="n_downsides">Class 3 (AHP). Whole plant highly toxic (CRC); overdose fatal (DEM). Too toxic to use (JAD; PH2). Some of the alkaloids transdermally dangerous (PH2).</data></node>
