<node id="hierba:dorema-ammoniacum-d-don-ammoniac"><data key="n_label">Ammoniac</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">AMMONIAC</data><data key="n_page">26</data><data key="n_scientific">Dorema ammoniacum D. Don</data><data key="n_safety">+</data><data key="n_safety_raw">+</data><data key="n_dosages">300–1000 mg ammoniacum (powdered gum resin) (PNC).</data><data key="n_downsides">Not covered (AHP). Emmenagogue folklore may contraindicate in pregnancy (PH2); folklore said to induce visual disturbances such as glaucoma (PH2). “Health hazards not known with proper therapeutic dosages” (PH2).</data></node>
