<node id="hierba:phellodendron-amurense-rupr-amur-corktree"><data key="n_label">Amur Corktree</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">AMUR CORKTREE</data><data key="n_page">27</data><data key="n_scientific">Phellodendron amurense Rupr.</data><data key="n_safety">++</data><data key="n_safety_raw">++</data><data key="n_dosages">3–10 g powdered bark/day (AKT); 1–3 g bark/day (HHB); 1–3 g 4:1 dry decoction (AKT).</data><data key="n_downsides">Class 2b (AHP). Not covered (BGB, PH2). One case of rash associated with ingestion (AHP). Good and bad effects of berberine may accrue to this species. Contains up to 25,000 ppm berberine, P. chinese, up to 80,000.</data></node>
