<node id="hierba:mercurialis-annua-l-annual-mercury"><data key="n_label">Annual Mercury</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">ANNUAL MERCURY</data><data key="n_page">33</data><data key="n_scientific">Mercurialis annua L.</data><data key="n_safety">+</data><data key="n_safety_raw">+</data><data key="n_dosages">No recent dosage found. I’d not advise the dosage repeated in Madaus (30–100 g sap/day). I usually caution against white sap.</data><data key="n_downsides">Not covered (AHP). Slightly poisonous; poisonings, including fatal ones, are known only among animals (PHR). Can lead to diarrhea and overactive bladder. Overdoses may lead to toxicity with diarrhea, hepatosis, nephrosis, neurosis, and paralysis (PH2). Pyridone derivatives may color the urine red (PH2).</data></node>
