<node id="hierba:terminalia-arjuna-arjuna"><data key="n_label">Arjuna</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_description">Sinónimos: Pentaptera arjuna Roxb. ex DC.</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">ARJUNA</data><data key="n_page">36</data><data key="n_scientific">Terminalia arjuna (Roxb. ex DC.) Wight &amp; Arn.</data><data key="n_safety">+</data><data key="n_safety_raw">+</data><data key="n_dosages">1–3 g bark (KAP); 3.88 g powdered bark (PH2); 1 g dry bark/day or 2–6 ml extract (1:2) (KEB); 14–28 ml decoction (KAP).</data><data key="n_downsides">Not covered (AHP; KOM). “Health hazards not known with proper therapeutic dosages” (PH2). One case of acute myocardial infarction tentatively associated with use of arjuna (KEB).</data></node>
