<node id="hierba:chenopodium-vulvaria-l-arrach"><data key="n_label">Arrach</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">ARRACH</data><data key="n_page">38</data><data key="n_scientific">Chenopodium vulvaria L.</data><data key="n_safety">++</data><data key="n_safety_raw">++</data><data key="n_downsides">Not covered (AHP). “Hazards and/or side effects not known for proper therapeutic dosages” (PH2).</data></node>
<node id="hierba:strophanthus-sarmentosus-dc-arrow-poison"><data key="n_label">Arrow-Poison</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">ARROW-POISON</data><data key="n_page">38</data><data key="n_scientific">Strophanthus sarmentosus DC.</data><data key="n_safety">X</data><data key="n_safety_raw">X</data><data key="n_dosages">Don’t take except with physician guidance! (JAD). Cymarin 0.6–0.9 mg ivn man/day, 2.3–2.5 mg orl man (HDN); Ouabain 0.25–0.65 mg ivn man/day, 12–48 mg/day orl man (HDN); K-Strophanthoside 0.2–1.2 mg ivn man/day, to 7.5 mg/day orl man; Toxic Dose 143 mg/man (HDN).</data><data key="n_downsides">Not covered (AHP). “Health hazards not known with proper therapeutic dosages” (PH2). Side effects may include cardiac arrhythmia, headache, ophthalmia (disturbance of color vision), queasiness, stupor, and vomiting. May enhance effects and side effects with calcium salts, glucocorticoids, laxatives, quinidine, and saluretics (PH2).</data></node>
