<node id="hierba:maranta-arundinacea-l-arrowroot"><data key="n_label">Arrowroot</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">ARROWROOT</data><data key="n_page">39</data><data key="n_scientific">Maranta arundinacea L.</data><data key="n_safety">+++</data><data key="n_safety_raw">+++</data><data key="n_dosages">2–3 drachms boiled in 1 pint milk or water (FEL); 15 g starch dissolved in 250 cc sweet water for dysentery (JFM).</data><data key="n_downsides">Class 1 (AHP). “Hazards and/or side effects not known for proper therapeutic dosages” (PH2) (but PH2 designates no specific quantified dosage! JAD). Canadian law disallows as nonmedicinal ingredient for oral products (AHP).</data></node>
