<node id="hierba:myroxylon-balsamum-balsam-of-peru"><data key="n_label">Balsam Of Peru</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_description">Sinónimos: Myrospermum pereirae Royle, Myroxylon pereirae (Royle) Klotzsch, Toluifera pereirae (Royle) Baill.</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">BALSAM OF PERU</data><data key="n_page">53</data><data key="n_scientific">Myroxylon balsamum (L.) Harms var. pereirae (Royle) Harms</data><data key="n_safety">++</data><data key="n_safety_raw">++</data><data key="n_dosages">0.2–2 g/day (MAD). Galenics with 5–20% balsam, no more than 10% if to be applied over a large area (PIP).</data><data key="n_downsides">Allergic skin reactions (KOM; PIP). Commission E reports contraindications: allergic disposition; adverse effects: allergic skin reactions. Application on large surfaces maximum 10%. Not to be used for more than 1 week (AEH).</data></node>
