<node id="hierba:actaea-spicata-l-baneberry"><data key="n_label">Baneberry</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_description">Sinónimos: A. spicata var. nigra L.</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">BANEBERRY</data><data key="n_page">56</data><data key="n_scientific">Actaea spicata L.</data><data key="n_safety">X</data><data key="n_safety_raw">X</data><data key="n_dosages">I discourage its use by anyone except skilled herbal practitioners.</data><data key="n_downsides">Not covered (AHP; KOM). “Hazards and/or side effects not known for proper therapeutic dosages” (PH2) (but PH2 designates no specific quantified dosage! JAD). Poisonous, possibly fatal (WO2), internally causing colic, delirium, dizziness, dyspnea, enteritis, gastritis, nausea, and vomiting (HHB; WO2).</data></node>
