<node id="hierba:pinellia-ternata-ban-xia"><data key="n_label">Ban Xia</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_description">Sinónimos: Arisaema cochinchinense Blume, Arum dracontium Lour., A. ternatum Thunb., P. cochinchinense (Blume) W. Wight, P. wawrae Engl.</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">BAN XIA</data><data key="n_page">56</data><data key="n_scientific">Pinellia ternata (Thunb.) Makino</data><data key="n_safety">+</data><data key="n_safety_raw">+</data><data key="n_dosages">2–6 g/day powdered processed root (AKT).</data><data key="n_downsides">Class 2b, 2d; contraindicated in all cases of bleeding or blood disorders (AHP). Not covered (KOM; PH2). Must be processed prior to use, cooking with ginger, vinegar, and/or alum (AKT). Not for long-term use, nor in pregnancy (AKT).</data></node>
