<node id="hierba:dioscorea-composita-hemsl-barbasco"><data key="n_label">Barbasco</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_description">Sinónimos: D. terpinapensis Uline ex R. Knuth.</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">BARBASCO</data><data key="n_page">57</data><data key="n_scientific">Dioscorea composita Hemsl.</data><data key="n_safety">+</data><data key="n_safety_raw">+</data><data key="n_downsides">Not covered (AHP; KOM; PHR). “Tubers are bitter and toxic. Steroidal drugs may produce serious side effects in the long run” (CRC). Diosgenin is converted by chemical means and elaborate processing to provide the final products that relieve arthrosis, asthma, and eczema, and to regulate metabolism and control fertility.</data></node>
