<node id="hierba:styrax-benzoin-dryander-benzoin"><data key="n_label">Benzoin</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">BENZOIN</data><data key="n_page">71</data><data key="n_scientific">Styrax benzoin Dryander.</data><data key="n_safety">++</data><data key="n_safety_raw">++</data><data key="n_dosages">For topical Friar's or Turlington's Balsam (each 100 ml contains an alcohol extract from 10 g benzoin, 8 g storax, 4 g balsam of Tolu and 2 g aloe); for cold sores, cracked skin, and indolent ulcers (BIB).</data><data key="n_downsides">Class 1 (AHP). Not Covered (PHR).</data></node>
