<node id="hierba:trillium-erectum-l-bethroot"><data key="n_label">Bethroot</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">BETHROOT</data><data key="n_page">74</data><data key="n_scientific">Trillium erectum L.</data><data key="n_safety">+</data><data key="n_safety_raw">+</data><data key="n_dosages">2–4 g root (HHB; PH2); 0.5–1 g powdered root (PNC); 4–8 ml liquid extract (PNC).</data><data key="n_downsides">Class 2b (AHP). As an emmenagogue/uterotonic, should not be used by pregnant mothers (AHP). “Hazards and/or side effects not known for proper therapeutic dosages” (PH2). In high doses emetic, emmenagogue, even promoting labor (PHR).</data></node>
