<node id="hierba:nigella-sativa-l-black-cumin"><data key="n_label">Black Cumin</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">BLACK CUMIN</data><data key="n_page">88</data><data key="n_scientific">Nigella sativa L.</data><data key="n_safety">++</data><data key="n_safety_raw">++</data><data key="n_dosages">0.6–1.2 g seed (HHB; MAD); 1 tsp seed in hot tea (MAD).</data><data key="n_extracts">Nigellone protects guinea pigs from histamine-induced bronchospasms (WOI). LD50 alcoholic extract 540–580 mg/kg ipr mouse (MPI).</data></node>
