<node id="hierba:ribes-nigrum-l-black-currant-fruit"><data key="n_label">Black Currant Fruit</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_description">Sinónimos: Ribes nigrum var. chlorocarpum Späth. Entries are for fruits rather than seeds; seed oil is a by-product! For leaves, see next entry. Leaves not generally considered food.</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">BLACK CURRANT FRUIT</data><data key="n_page">89</data><data key="n_scientific">Ribes nigrum L.</data><data key="n_safety">+++</data><data key="n_safety_raw">+++</data><data key="n_dosages">600–6000 mg/day; 4 (250 mg) capsules 2 ×/day; 1–2 tsp chopped leaf, up to several ×/day (APA); 5–10 ml fruit syrup, 1–several ×/day (PHR; PH2); 1 glassful fruit juice/day; gargle with 1 part juice/1 part water (PHR).</data><data key="n_downsides">Class 1 (AHP). Not covered by Commission E (KOM). None known (PHR). Not covered (CAN).</data><data key="n_extracts">As a major source of the major COX-2 Inhibitor ([+]-catechin), this might be viewed by enthusiasts as another herbal miracle aspirin (COX). Anthocyanins and polyphenols in berries of several Ribes, Rubus, and Vaccinium spp. have in vitro antiradical activity on chemically generated superoxide radicals. The extracts also inhibit xanthine oxidase. All crude extracts were highly active toward chemically generated superoxide radicals. Ribes nigrum extracts exhibited most activity, being the richest in both anthocyanins and polyphenols. But Ribes rubrum extracts seem to contain more active substances (X1332092).</data></node>
<node id="act:angioprotective"><data key="n_label">Angioprotective</data><data key="n_type">Actividad</data><data key="n_description">Citada en 2 monografías</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">Activities</data></node>
