<node id="hierba:bletilla-striata-bletilla"><data key="n_label">Bletilla, Hardy Orchid</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_description">Sinónimos: Bletia hyacinthina (J. E. Smith) R. Br.; Cymbidium hyacinthinum J. E. Smith; Epidendrum tuberosum Lour.; Limodorum striatum Thunb.</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">BLETILLA, HARDY ORCHID</data><data key="n_page">102</data><data key="n_scientific">Bletilla striata (Thunb.) Rchb. f.</data><data key="n_safety">++</data><data key="n_safety_raw">++</data><data key="n_dosages">3–9(–16) g dry root (FAY); 5–10 g powdered root in decoction (FAY).</data><data key="n_downsides">Not covered (AHP; KOM; PH2). Not for use in chronic lung ailments. Large or frequent dosage can become toxic. Take root only with medical supervision (FAY).</data></node>
