<node id="hierba:ranunculus-bulbosus-l-bulbous-buttercup"><data key="n_label">Bulbous Buttercup</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">BULBOUS BUTTERCUP</data><data key="n_page">124</data><data key="n_scientific">Ranunculus bulbosus L.</data><data key="n_safety">+</data><data key="n_safety_raw">+</data><data key="n_dosages">Homeopathic (PH2).</data><data key="n_downsides">Not covered (AHP). “Hazards and/or side effects not known for proper therapeutic dosages” (PH2) (but PH2 designates no specific quantified dosage! JAD). Contraindicated “absolutely” in pregnancy (PHR; PH2). Protoanemonin with significant antiseptic activity on aerobes, anaerobes, dermatophytes, and yeast, including MDR pathogens.</data></node>
