<node id="hierba:myrciaria-dubia-camu-camu"><data key="n_label">Camu-Camu</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_description">Sinónimos: M. paraensis O. Berg, Psidium dubium Kunth.</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">CAMU-CAMU</data><data key="n_page">143</data><data key="n_scientific">Myrciaria dubia (Kunth) McVaugh</data><data key="n_safety">+++</data><data key="n_safety_raw">+++</data><data key="n_dosages">Food farmacy, 3–4 fruits providing 300–400 mg vitamin C (JAD).</data><data key="n_downsides">Not covered (AHP; KOM; PH2). Most FNF entries above based on the fact that camu-camu is a very rich edible source of vitamin C.</data></node>
