<node id="hierba:acacia-catechu-catechu"><data key="n_label">Catechu, Black Cutch</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_description">Sinónimos: Mimosa catechu L. f.</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">CATECHU, BLACK CUTCH</data><data key="n_page">162</data><data key="n_scientific">Acacia catechu (L. f.) Willd.</data><data key="n_safety">++</data><data key="n_safety_raw">++</data><data key="n_dosages">5–20 grains to 1 drachm gum, only 1–4 grains as expectorant (DEP). 0.3–2 g gum to 3 ×/day (PH2).</data><data key="n_downsides">Not covered (AHP). “Hazards and/or side effects not known for proper therapeutic dosages” (PH2). But 100 years ago, “Believed to be anaphrodisiac and to cause impotence when used in excess” (DEP).</data></node>
