<node id="hierba:agave-sisalana-perrine-mescal"><data key="n_label">Mescal</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">MESCAL</data><data key="n_page">499</data><data key="n_scientific">Agave sisalana Perrine</data><data key="n_safety">++</data><data key="n_safety_raw">++</data></node>
<node id="hierba:sophora-secundiflora-mescal-bean"><data key="n_label">Mescal Bean</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">MESCAL BEAN</data><data key="n_page">499</data><data key="n_scientific">Sophora secundiflora (Ortega) Lag. ex DC.</data><data key="n_safety">+</data><data key="n_safety_raw">+</data><data key="n_downsides">Not covered (AHP). Seed and flower poisonous, possibly causing convulsions and nausea, death due to respiratory failure (asphyxia). One chewed seed can kill a child (CRC).</data></node>
<node id="hierba:prosopis-juliflora-mesquite"><data key="n_label">Mesquite</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">MESQUITE</data><data key="n_page">499</data><data key="n_scientific">Prosopis juliflora (Sw.) DC.</data><data key="n_safety">+++</data><data key="n_safety_raw">+++</data></node>
<node id="hierba:datura-metel-l-metel"><data key="n_label">Metel, Hindu Datura</data><data key="n_type">Hierba</data><data key="n_source">Duke JA et al. Handbook of Medicinal Herbs, 2nd ed. CRC Press, 2002</data><data key="n_chapter">Catalog of Herbs (A to Z)</data><data key="n_section">METEL, HINDU DATURA</data><data key="n_page">500</data><data key="n_scientific">Datura metel L.</data><data key="n_safety">X</data><data key="n_safety_raw">X</data><data key="n_downsides">Not covered (AHP). “See D. stramonium” (CRC). Linnaeus is suggested to have said that this might be preferable to stramonium (DEP).</data></node>
